### 4.2 Backend — REST API Endpoints

The following API groups have been implemented and are fully functional:

- **Authentication** — Login (`/auth/login/`), token refresh, `/me/` profile
- **Admin APIs** — Dashboard overview, user management, appointment management, shift management, remote vitals monitoring, inpatient order review, remote referrals
- **Doctor APIs** — Dashboard stats, appointment management, workbench (consultations, prescriptions), inpatient orders, remote vitals monitoring
- **Nurse APIs** — Patient queue, vitals recording, task management, prescription administration, medication schedule queue
- **Patient APIs** — Profile view/edit, appointment booking and cancellation, vitals history, prescriptions, admission status, medical history
- **Messaging** — Conversation and message management
- **Utility** — User search, avatar upload, notifications

### 4.3 Frontend — Pages & Components

**Authentication**
- Login page with JWT token storage and role-based redirect
- Protected route component that guards all dashboard pages

**Admin Dashboard** (`/admin/`)
- Overview dashboard with system-wide statistics
- Full **User Management** (create, edit, deactivate users)
- **Appointment Management** (view, reassign, update status)
- **Admissions** management panel
- **Inpatient Orders** review and approval
- **Remote Referrals / Monitoring** panel
- **Reports** section

**Doctor Dashboard** (`/doctor/`)
- Overview dashboard with personal stats (today's appointments, pending vitals, etc.)
- **Doctor Workbench** — Full clinical consultation interface: vitals review, clinical notes, diagnosis, treatment plan, prescription builder
- **Appointment Management** — Accept/reject appointments, manage schedule
- **Inpatients** — View admitted patients and manage their orders
- **Remote Monitoring** — Review vitals submitted by remote patients
- **Doctor Requests** — Manage pending patient requests
- **Messaging** — In-app messaging with colleagues
- **Patient History** — Complete patient record view

**Nurse Dashboard** (`/nurse/`)
- Overview dashboard with queue and task summary
- **Medications panel** — Medication schedule queue with administration tracking
- **Prescriptions Panel** — Review and action active prescriptions

**Patient Dashboard** (`/patient/`)
- Comprehensive tabbed portal featuring:
  - My Appointments (book, view, cancel)
  - My Vitals history
  - My Prescriptions
  - My Admission status
  - My Medical History
  - Profile editing modal (`PatientProfileEditModal`)

**Shared Components**
- Reusable [Layout.jsx](file:///c:/Users/USER/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/HosiKe/frontend/src/components/Layout.jsx) with collapsible sidebar and role-aware navigation
- `Spinner`, `ProtectedRoute`, and other common UI components

---

## 5. Current Project Status

> **Overall Completion: ~90%**

The core system is fully functional end-to-end. All four role dashboards are implemented, connected to the backend, and verified to work with demo accounts. The application can be run locally with:

```bash
# Backend
cd backend && python manage.py runserver

# Frontend
cd frontend && npm run dev
```

Demo accounts are seeded via `python manage.py seed_data`:

| Role | Username | Password |
|------|----------|----------|
| Admin | admin1 | pass1234 |
| Doctor | doctor1 | pass1234 |
| Nurse | nurse1 | pass1234 |
| Patient | patient1 | pass1234 |

---

## 6. Challenges Encountered

| Challenge | Resolution |
|-----------|------------|
| JWT token refresh on expired sessions | Implemented Axios interceptor to auto-refresh tokens |
| Role-based routing with React Router | Built `ProtectedRoute` component that reads user role and redirects accordingly |
| Nested serializer validation for prescriptions | Fixed `InpatientOrderSerializer` to handle nested `medication_items` correctly |
| Managing complex appointment state machine | Defined explicit status choices and transitions at the model level |
| Real-time messaging without WebSockets | Implemented polling-based message refresh in the chat UI |
| Inpatient medication scheduling | Designed a [MedicationSchedule](file:///c:/Users/USER/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/HosiKe/backend/api/models.py#239-260) model linked to [MedicationItem](file:///c:/Users/USER/OneDrive/Desktop/Projects/HosiKe/backend/api/models.py#228-238) for granular tracking |

